YZE","contextFamily":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_MELTING_06","statement":"Ice melted in a warm room and no new material was measured. Which criterion should guide the analysis?","options":["A new gas was proven.","Describe what changed without adding an unmeasured chemical claim.","The mass necessarily disappeared.","The room became colder because of the ice."],"correctAnswer":"Describe what changed without adding an unmeasured chemical claim.","explanation":"The answer uses the relevant evidence and keeps the conclusion within the conditions described in the situation.","hint":"Identify the comparison, evidence or condition before choosing an answer.","errorFocus":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION","misconceptions":{"A new gas was proven.":["V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION"]},"position":13},{"id":"v6-science-evidence-conclusion-expansion-07","purpose":"PRACTICE","difficulty":"MEDIUM","cognitiveProcess":"COMPARE","contextFamily":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_MELTING_07","statement":"Ice melted in a warm room and no new material was measured. How can the same reasoning be transferred to another situation?","options":["A new gas was proven.","The mass necessarily disappeared.","Separate direct observations from explanations in another material change.","The room became colder because of the ice."],"correctAnswer":"Separate direct observations from explanations in another material change.","explanation":"The answer uses the relevant evidence and keeps the conclusion within the conditions described in the situation.","hint":"Identify the comparison, evidence or condition before choosing an answer.","errorFocus":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION","misconceptions":{"A new gas was proven.":["V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION"]},"position":14},{"id":"v6-science-evidence-conclusion-expansion-08","purpose