swer uses the relevant evidence and keeps the conclusion within the conditions described in the situation.","hint":"Identify the comparison, evidence or condition before choosing an answer.","errorFocus":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION","misconceptions":{"More variables always make a test stronger.":["V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION"]},"position":22},{"id":"v6-science-evidence-conclusion-expansion-16","purpose":"PRACTICE","difficulty":"MEDIUM","cognitiveProcess":"APPLY","contextFamily":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CONTROL_16","statement":"A student tests soap brands but changes the amount of water and scrubbing time between trials. Which conclusion should be avoided without more information?","options":["More variables always make a test stronger.","Soap cannot be investigated.","The result is certain because it was repeated once.","Treat any difference as proof that the soap caused it."],"correctAnswer":"Treat any difference as proof that the soap caused it.","explanation":"The answer uses the relevant evidence and keeps the conclusion within the conditions described in the situation.","hint":"Identify the comparison, evidence or condition before choosing an answer.","errorFocus":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION","misconceptions":{"More variables always make a test stronger.":["V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_CRITERION_OR_SCOPE_CONFUSION"]},"position":23},{"id":"v6-science-evidence-conclusion-expansion-17","purpose":"TRANSFER","difficulty":"HARD","cognitiveProcess":"EVALUATE","contextFamily":"V6_SCIENCE-EVIDENCE-CONCLUSION-EXPANSION_OBSERVATION_17","statement":"A thermometer reads 28 degrees Celsius, and a student writes that the room feels uncomfortable to everyone. What distinction is needed?","options":["The temperature is a measurement; discomfort is an interpretation that may vary among people.","Temperature cannot be measure